This software statically links to FFmpeg libraries (<http://ffmpeg.org/>).
FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) version
2.1 or later by default, but the license of a build depends on how it's
configured:

- With --enable-gpl, and GPL components such as x264 or x265, it's licensed
  under the GNU General Public License (GPL), and so is a binary which
  includes it.
- With --enable-nonfree, and nonfree components such as fdk-aac, FFmpeg's
  configure reports its license as "nonfree and unredistributable", and a
  binary which includes it can't be redistributed.

The Makefile configures FFmpeg with --enable-gpl and --enable-nonfree, and
links x264, x265 and fdk-aac when they're found, so a binary built with it is
for your own use, and can't be redistributed. The license of a build is
FFMPEG_LICENSE in build/ffmpeg-<version>/config.h. To distribute binaries,
configure FFmpeg without --enable-nonfree, which is a GPL build, or without
--enable-gpl too, which is an LGPL build.

